  "worked_solution": "Suppose $a$ and $b$ are two lines. Then,\n\n- $a∥b$ means $a$ and $b$ are parallel, and\n\n- $a⊥b$ means $a$ and $b$ are perpendicular.\n\nIn the given diagram, there are two pairs of perpendicular lines:\n\n- $s$ is perpendicular to $t,$ which we write as $s⊥t$\n\n- $w$ is perpendicular to $t,$ which we write as $w⊥t.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14151975/assets/756f579f20695c46394e6667fd78444504b1470619ea6ca4b68eed87eeed934e.png)\n\nTherefore, the correct statement is $s⊥t$ and $w⊥t.$",
